    "explanation": "Nova is a good choice on 2-lane Battlegrounds as they do not require a high amount of waveclear and they give her many opportunities to gank isolated enemy Heroes who tend to expose in the solo lane (such as Hanamura Temple).\n\nDue to her lack of waveclear, Nova is usually a bad choice on 3-lane Battlegrounds, especially if their Objective takes too long for her high Mana consumption to not be an issue (for example Alterac Pass) and/or requires to kill multiple Monsters at the same time (such as Infernal Shrines)."
  },
  "builds": [
    {
      "name": "Holo Decoy Build",
      "label": "Recommended",
      "description": "Nova's Holo Decoy Build provides good single-target sustain damage from the mid game. Since you cannot choose the target of your Clones, this Build is more effective against partially or fully isolated enemy Heroes.\n\nLethal Decoy at Level 16 increases your damage output when having Clones active, although you cannot choose who they will attack. Rapid Projection at Level 4 lets you do this more often and for less Mana. Ionic Force Field at Level 13 makes you and your Clones harder to kill.\n\nAt Level 20, Rewind is the best option for burst damage, Precision Barrage provides more waveclear and area of effect damage, and Apollo Suit to confuse enemies with Stealth.",
